{"id":129,"number":74,"symbol":"Ecad","name":"Cadherin-1 (E-cadherin)","gene":"CDH1","family":"STR","location":"P","other_locations":[],"cell_rank":0,"mass_kda":97.5,"length_aa":882,"discovery_year":1977,"milestone":"Calcium-dependent cell adhesion described (Takeichi)","blurb":"Zips neighbouring epithelial cells together; lost when cancers spread.","drugs":[],"therapeutic":null,"pathways":[],"orthologs":{"ecoli":null,"human":"CDH1","mouse":"Cdh1"},"variant_count":1,"misfolded":null,"uniprot_id":"P12830","function":"Cadherins are calcium-dependent cell adhesion proteins. They preferentially interact with themselves in a homophilic manner in connecting cells; cadherins may thus contribute to the sorting of heterogeneous cell types. CDH1 is involved in mechanisms regulating cell-cell adhesions, mobility and proliferation of epithelial cells. Promotes organization of radial actin fiber structure and cellular response to contractile forces, via its interaction with AMOTL2 which facilitates anchoring of radial actin fibers to CDH1 junction complexes at the cell membrane. Plays a role in the early stages of desmosome cell-cell junction formation via facilitating the recruitment of DSG2 and DSP to desmosome plaques. Has a potent invasive suppressor role. It is a ligand for integrin alpha-E/beta-7","sequence":"","pdb_ids":["2OMZ","2OMX","2OMY","1O6S","2OMU","3FF7","2OMV","8H62","4ZT1","2O72","2OMT","3FF8"],"alphafold_url":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P12830-F1-model_v6.pdb","variants":[{"change":"Germline loss of function","disease":"Hereditary diffuse gastric cancer","note":null}],"partners":[{"id":131,"symbol":"Bcat","name":"Catenin beta-1 (β-catenin)","score":0.999,"effect_out":"inhibits","effect_in":null},{"id":68,"symbol":"Egfr","name":"Epidermal growth factor receptor","score":0.999,"effect_out":"regulates","effect_in":null},{"id":44,"symbol":"Mdm2","name":"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase Mdm2","score":0.997,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":null},{"id":17,"symbol":"